        ]
      },
      "id": "BD92D2A8B8",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "35",
        "end": "35",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 42,
        "text": "Here we are, back to our hero, the oyster.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A3FB771B11",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "36",
        "end": "36",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 48,
        "text": "And again, it's this incredibly exciting animal.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "F7E0F2AF44",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "37",
        "end": "37",
        "startOffset": 59,
        "endOffset": 79,
        "text": "beautiful, glamorous",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "86A4CBE0D9",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "37",
        "end": "37",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 141,
        "text": "It accepts algae and detritus in one end, and through this beautiful, glamorous set of stomach organs, out the other end comes cleaner water.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "7780565C3C",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "38",
        "end": "38",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 58,
        "text": "And one oyster can filter up to 50 gallons of water a day.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "7D99F0B3C1",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "39",
        "end": "39",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 126,
        "text": "Oyster reefs also covered about a quarter of our harbor and were capable of filtering water in the harbor in a matter of days.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "60DAD51294",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "40",
        "end": "40",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 45,
        "text": "They were key in our culture and our economy.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "EB01770094",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "41",
        "end": "41",
        "startOffset": 24,
        "endOffset": 55,
        "text": "built on the backs of oystermen",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "B909C2D79A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "41",
        "end": "41",
        "startOffset": 78,
        "endOffset": 112,
        "text": "literally built over oyster shells",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "B5B5EDCD80",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "41",
        "end": "41",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 113,
        "text": "Basically, New York was built on the backs of oystermen, and our streets were literally built over oyster shells.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "E66B34832A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "42",
        "end": "42",
        "startOffset": 55,
        "endOffset": 96,
        "text": "as ubiquitous as the hotdog cart is today",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "34C4A4C968",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "42",
        "end": "42",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 97,
        "text": "This image is an image of an oyster cart, which is now as ubiquitous as the hotdog cart is today.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "90779DE814",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "43",
        "end": "43",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 49,
        "text": "So again, we got the short end of the deal there.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "4398CBEA5C",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "44",
        "end": "44",
        "startOffset": 11,
        "endOffset": 121,
        "text": "Finally, oysters can attenuate and agglomerate onto each other and form these amazing natural reef structures.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "EC87C9949A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "45",
        "end": "45",
        "startOffset": 19,
        "endOffset": 44,
        "text": "nature's wave attenuators",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D311E192CE",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "46",
        "end": "46",
        "startOffset": 20,
        "endOffset": 27,
        "text": "bedrock",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "46097AFB67",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "47",
        "end": "47",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 34,
        "text": "Many, many species depend on them.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "825015FD16",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 91,
        "text": "So we were inspired by the oyster, but I was also inspired by the life cycle of the oyster.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "AB3FB9301E",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "49",
        "end": "49",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 212,
        "text": "It can move from a fertilized egg to a spat, which is when they're floating through the water, and when they're ready to attach onto another oyster, to an adult male oyster or female oyster, in a number of weeks.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "4610866B20",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "50",
        "end": "50",
        "startOffset": 85,
        "endOffset": 105,
